[{:db/id 17592186142747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a0f6eeb8-92d5-597f-8a13-0df97ae1dcbd" "question-f9b7769c-50a8-5c21-9b7b-d88c90ff5615" "question-96170013-5e0f-501d-81cf-eceefbf4bc14" "question-622b729f-d637-5751-a87a-e7dfc82fcd52"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142644 :question/problem "What is the value of $\\dfrac 1 6 \\div 5 ?$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\color{blue}5$ is $\\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{5}}}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}5} = \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply the fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 6 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac {1\\times 1} {6\\times 5} = \\dfrac{1}{30}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142748 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5d19cf10-06a4-535a-918f-99e1c41cec3a" "question-55d5c75e-f419-5763-b188-8a0bd660c4bc" "question-d85851be-27b4-56f8-847b-44fecabf63b0" "question-116aa339-f102-5c92-bdf9-67bd12e3af27" "question-69c05136-433e-5b89-9890-65d169f7fcba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142645 :question/problem "What is the values of $\\dfrac 2 3 \\div 7 ?$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\color{blue}7$ is $\\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{7}}}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 2 3\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}7} = \\dfrac 2 3\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}7} .\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 2 3 \\times \\dfrac{1}{7} = \\dfrac {2\\times 1} {3\\times 7} = \\dfrac{2}{21}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142749 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4aa4d485-027c-5fe5-b786-8809344ecf97" "question-c1a99f57-fa06-5739-b60a-94b0deccc6fc" "question-6f5dde03-85f8-5a5a-89d7-edf27b23e39d" "question-563011eb-aedf-54fc-b79c-67413e9b63b6" "question-4d44aca2-82e0-5f20-ace0-bbb17307dbfa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142646 :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{6}{11} \\div 3 .$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\color{blue}3$ is $\\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{3}}}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {6}{11} \\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}3} =  \\dfrac {6}{11}\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {6}{11} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac {6\\times 1} {11\\times 3} = \\dfrac{6}{33}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{6}{33} = \\dfrac{6\\div 3}{33\\div 3} = \\dfrac{2}{11}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0f6eeb8-92d5-597f-8a13-0df97ae1dcbd" :question/id #uuid "a0f6eeb8-92d5-597f-8a13-0df97ae1dcbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-57233" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{8}÷4=$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $4$ is $\\frac{1}{4}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\,÷\\,4=\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 1}{8\\times 4}=\\frac{1}{32}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-10da6a0a-6ccf-5531-a8dd-176ac67a201b"] :db/ensure [: